## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design offline-first, distributed data synchronization with real-world constraints (latency, privacy, scale) in a mobile fleet context. Emphasizes secure, conflict-aware replication without centralized bottlenecks.

## Key Concepts
- WebRTC DataChannels for direct device sync
- CRDT-based namespaces for idempotent merges
- Vector clocks for causality, tombstones for deletes
- End-to-end encryption and minimal key management
- Garbage collection strategy for tombstones and stale data

## Code Example
```javascript
// useP2PQueue.ts
import { useState, useEffect } from 'react';
import { P2PSyncManager } from './syncManager';

export const useP2PQueue = () => {
  const [pendingOps, setPendingOps] = useState([]);
  const [isConnected, setIsConnected] = useState(false);

  useEffect(() => {
    const sync = new P2PSyncManager();
    sync.onConnectionChange(setIsConnected);
    sync.onPendingOpsChange(setPendingOps);
    return () => sync.disconnect();
  }, []);

  const enqueue = async (namespace, operation) => {
    await syncManager.enqueueOperation(namespace, operation);
  };

  return { pendingOps, isConnected, enqueue };
};
```

## Trade-offs
- **Latency**: Direct P2P reduces round-trip time vs cloud relay
- **Privacy**: Data stays on-device, no third-party exposure
- **Scalability**: Mesh topology scales linearly but requires connection management

## Why This Is Asked

Tests practical RN skills: building reusable components, accessibility across platforms, and theming with Appearance API, plus a small hook pattern.

## Key Concepts

- Accessibility props (accessibilityLabel, accessibilityHint, accessibilityRole)
- Theming with Appearance/useColorScheme and React Context
- Custom hook useTheme and ThemeProvider
- Performance considerations for re-renders and memoization

## Code Example

```javascript
import React, {createContext, useContext, useMemo, useState} from 'react';
import {Pressable, Text} from 'react-native';

export const ThemeContext = createContext('light');
export const useTheme = () => useContext(ThemeContext);

export function ThemeProvider({children}) {
  // Simplified example; in real code use Appearance or useColorScheme
  const [scheme] = useState('light');
  const value = useMemo(() => ({scheme}), [scheme]);
  return <ThemeContext.Provider value={value}>{children}</ThemeContext.Provider>;
}

function Card({title, price}) {
  const {scheme} = useTheme();
  const bg = scheme === 'dark' ? '#222' : '#fff';
  return (
    <Pressable accessibilityLabel={title}
               accessibilityHint="View details"
               accessibilityRole="button"
               style={{backgroundColor: bg}}>
      <Text>{title}</Text>
      <Text>{price}</Text>
    </Pressable>
  );
}
```

